{"name":"Sacrifice Altar","hex":"#850101","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sacrifice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Originally, the killing (and often burning) of a human being or an animal as an offering to a deity; later, also the offering of an object to a deity.\n\nA human being or an animal, or a physical object or immaterial thing (see etymology 1 sense 1.3), offered to a deity.\n\n The offering of devotion, penitence, prayer, thanksgiving, etc., to a deity.\n\n\nJesus Christ's voluntary offering of himself to God the Father to be crucified as atonement for the sins of humankind.\n The rite of Holy Communion or the Mass, regarded as  an offering of thanksgiving to God for Christ's crucifixion, or  a perpetual re-presentation of Christ's sacrificial offering.","Originally, the killing (and often burning) of a human being or an animal as an offering to a deity; later, also the offering of an object to a deity."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To offer (a human being or an animal, or an object) to a deity.","To offer (a human being or an animal, or an object) to a deity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacrifice"},{"term":"altar","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A table or similar flat-topped structure used for religious rites.","A raised area around an altar in a church; the sanctuary."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/altar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sacrifice","blocks":[{"text":"Sacrifice is an act or offering made to a deity. A sacrifice can serve as propitiation, or a sacrifice can be an offering of praise and thanksgiving."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice_-_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_-_Musei_Capitolini_-_Rome_2016.jpg/330px-Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice_-_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_-_Musei_Capitolini_-_Rome_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacrifice","wikidata":"Q179723"},{"title":"Altar","blocks":[{"text":"An altar is a table or platform for the presentation of religious offerings, for sacrifices, or for other ritualistic purposes. Altars are found at shrines, temples, churches, and other places of worship. They are used particularly in Christianity, Buddhism, Hinduism, and modern paganism. Many historical-medieval faiths also made use of them, including the Roman, Greek, and Norse religions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/RD_alter.jpg/330px-RD_alter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Altar","wikidata":"Q101687"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Laurinm%C3%A4ki_sacrificial_cairn.JPG/500px-Laurinm%C3%A4ki_sacrificial_cairn.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Laurinm%C3%A4ki_sacrificial_cairn.JPG/1280px-Laurinm%C3%A4ki_sacrificial_cairn.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Laurinm%C3%A4ki_sacrificial_cairn.JPG/500px-Laurinm%C3%A4ki_sacrificial_cairn.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The sacrificial cairn in Janakkala, Finland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALaurinm%C3%A4ki_sacrificial_cairn.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Sacrifice_scene_Louvre_G402.jpg/500px-Sacrifice_scene_Louvre_G402.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Sacrifice_scene_Louvre_G402.jpg/1280px-Sacrifice_scene_Louvre_G402.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Sacr